    "body": "Reusing an existing Cython memoryview with a matching dtype bypasses buffer acquisition and its writability check, allowing writable typed memoryviews to reference read-only storage such as `bytes`.\n\nCheck the buffer’s `readonly` flag before accepting a writable conversion. Extend the existing memoryview doctest to cover read-only views and slices, plus an ordinary writable-view round trip.\n\nI'm working on improving the safety of Python's buffer protocol implementation. I made a demo using a read through a const Cython typed memoryview and a simultaneous write through a different buffer export, to show the flaw in the buffer protocol illustrated by Alex Gaynor here: https://alexgaynor.net/2022/oct/23/buffers-on-the-edge/.\n\nWhile working on this demo, I noticed that Cython is missing a check that allows writing into a read-only buffer. For example:\n\n```cython\n# cython: language_level=3\n\ndef as_const(const unsigned char[:] data):\n    return data\n\ndef overwrite(unsigned char[:] data):\n    data[0] = 100\n\ndata = bytes(bytearray(b\"abc\"))\nview = as_const(data)\n\nprint(\"before:\", data)\nprint(\"readonly:\", memoryview(view).readonly)\n\ntry:\n    overwrite(view)\nexcept ValueError as exc:\n    print(\"ValueError:\", exc)\n\nprint(\"after:\", data)\n```\n\nOn `cython` `master`, this program allows writing into a `bytes` and outputs:\n\n```\nbefore: b'abc'\nreadonly: True\nafter: b'dbc'\n```\n\nWith my patch, this program prints:\n\n```\nbefore: b'abc'\nreadonly: True\nValueError: Cannot create writable memory view from read-only memoryview\nafter: b'abc'\n```",
